{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-18_14-39-49-dragonboat_raft-real-run && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nout = {\n \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Record one ordering detail that the durability and read accounts both touch. engine.processSteps runs every active node once, applies snapshot updates, then sends the free-order messages and calls processReadyToRead, processDroppedEntries and processDroppedReadIndexes, and only afterwards calls logdb.SaveRaftState for the whole batch; the remaining messages, including vote responses, are sent by processRaftUpdate after that save. So ReadIndex readiness signals are released before the batch is persisted, while election-relevant responses wait for it. The read index a readiness signal carries refers to already-committed state, so this is an ordering fact rather than a stale-read observation.\\\",\n \\\"sources\\\": [\n  {\\\"id\\\": \\\"engine-process-steps\\\", \\\"file\\\": \\\"engine.go\\\", \\\"start_line\\\": 1287, \\\"end_line\\\": 1327, \\\"kind\\\": \\\"code_observation\\\"},\n  {\\\"id\\\": \\\"node-free-order-messages\\\", \\\"file\\\": \\\"node.go\\\", \\\"start_line\\\": 965, \\\"end_line\\\": 999, \\\"kind\\\": \\\"code_observation\\\"}\n ],\n \\\"knowledge\\\": [\n  {\n   \\\"ref\\\": \\\"@process-steps-free-order-before-save\\\",\n   \\\"kind\\\": \\\"behavior\\\",\n   \\\"statement\\\": \\\"engine.processSteps takes one update per active node, calls applySnapshotAndUpdate, then for each update sends the free-order messages (Replicate and Ping) and calls processReadyToRead, processDroppedEntries and processDroppedReadIndexes, and only after that calls logdb.SaveRaftState for the whole batch. The remaining messages, including vote responses and read-index replies, are released by node.processRaftUpdate after the save. Readiness signals therefore reach the node layer before the batch is persisted, while election-relevant responses do not.\\\",\n   \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"The updates come from the engine's batch loop, each node includes its changed raft state, and the log DB implements SaveRaftState as one atomically committed write batch.\\\",\n   \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"engine-process-steps\\\", \\\"node-free-order-messages\\\"]\n  }\n ]\n}\njson.dump(out, open('draft/update.json','w'), indent=2)\nopen('draft/update.json','a').write(\\\"\\\\n\\\")\nPY\ncd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance && .venv/bin/consensus-assurance validate --run runs/2026-10-18_14-39-49-dragonboat_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
